--TEST--
A written key type in a keyed `foreach` over a `Core\ObjectMap<K, V>` must accept `K`, so a key or value type the map does not have does not compile while a wider type such as `object` does — `rule:iteration/keyed-interfaces`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:iteration/keys-and-values-from-a-map
final class Tag {
    public string $name;

    public function constructor(string $name) {
        $this->name = $name;
    }
}

Core\ObjectMap<Tag, int> $weights = new Core\ObjectMap<Tag, int>();

// The keys are `Tag` objects, so a `string` key does not compile.
foreach ($weights as string $name => int $n) {
}

// The values are `int`, so a `string` value does not compile.
foreach ($weights as Tag $tag => string $text) {
}

// Every `Tag` is an `object`, so this key type compiles.
foreach ($weights as object $any => int $m) {
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `Tag`
   --> case.nvs:14:22
%A
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `int`
   --> case.nvs:18:34
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
